HyperPot — Monitor detection FIXED (27 Oct 2026)
================================================
Problem: the proactive monitor rebuilt the split spuriously even when the TUF
was alive.

Two flawed approaches found and discarded (honest record):
  1. TCP-probe the RPC port (50052): FALSE POSITIVE. ggml-rpc-server is
     single-client; while llama-server holds the RPC connection, an external
     probe is refused -> looks "dead" though it is working.
  2. Poll llama-server /health: FALSE POSITIVE. During a slow 3B split
     generation the server is busy and does not answer /health in time.

Correct signal (verified Phase 0): a truly dead remote node makes llama.cpp
ABORT -> the llama-server PROCESS EXITS. A busy/slow server is still running;
a dead-node server exits. So the monitor now watches PROCESS EXIT only
(s.running flips false via cmd.Wait()), no port/health probing.

Verified after fix:
  - Stability: TUF stays up, 3 big-tier prompts -> gen events = 1 (NO spurious
    rebuild), all answered via=big-3B-split from the live 2-way split.
  - Recovery: TUF killed -> llama-server exits -> monitor rebuilds gen 2 over
    [] (ROG alone) -> after-kill prompt answered ("Cat.").

Net: the big-tier split is now STABLE while healthy and RECOVERS on real death.
